@*
    The forms an Agent is waiting on, shown where the conversation that produced them happened
    (elicitation bridge, decisions E-5 and E-6). Mirrors QuestionCard: view state derived from in-memory
    server state (ElicitationStore.Get(roomId)), answered by an in-process call to ElicitationService -
    no Envelope. The answer is a Message from the Human; a card disappears on
    RoomEvents.ElicitationsChanged, and the outcome is never card state.

    Three things differ from QuestionCard. First, a Room can hold SEVERAL waiting cards (an Agent's
    AskUserQuestion, a refusal dialog, an MCP form), so every card is shown, in arrival order, each
    with the values the Human has entered into it. Second, the card is not held back while its asker
    is writing: the asker's Turn is open on purpose (it is waiting on this very form), so there is
    no D-8 gate and this component does not even inject Drafts. Third, the fields are typed, so the
    card holds what the Human typed as text - one list of entries per field key, exactly the shape
    ElicitationComposer reads (a scalar field zero or one entry, a multi select its chosen option
    values) - and ElicitationComposer.CanSend, not this component, decides when Send is enabled.

    Every text on the card (message, labels, descriptions, options, header) was written by a model or
    an MCP server, so it is rendered as plain text through Razor's own encoding. Never MarkupString,
    never Markdown.

    The busy set and the ElicitationsChanged subscription interact the way they do on QuestionCard:
    ElicitationService.AnswerAsync's first action is ElicitationStore.TryTake, which raises
    ElicitationsChanged synchronously, and this card is itself subscribed. OnElicitationsChanged ignores
    a fire while any answer is in flight, and the click handler's own finally block re-reads the store
    once the call returns, so a tap never hides the busy view before it can be seen, and another tab's
    change still updates normally.

    An AskUserQuestion question carries a companion "Other" text field (CustomAnswerFor). It is drawn
    under its question, and typing in it clears and disables that question's options - a typed answer
    beats a selection, exactly as the Adapter does.
*@
@implements IDisposable
@using System.Globalization
@using Agency.Huddle.App.Elicitation

@inject RoomEvents Events
@inject ElicitationStore Elicitations
@inject ElicitationService Service
@inject ITeamDirectory TeamDirectory
@inject ISnackbar Snackbar

@if (this.room is { Archived: false })
{
    foreach (PendingElicitation card in this.cards)
    {
        PendingElicitation current = card;
        bool busy = this.IsBusy(current);

        <MudPaper @key="current.Id" Outlined="true" Class="elicitation-card pa-3 my-2" role="region" aria-label="@($"Form from {current.AskerName}")">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="elicitation-card-title">@current.AskerName is asking</MudText>

            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(current.Form.Message) && !current.Form.MessageRepeatsLabel)
            {
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="elicitation-card-message">@current.Form.Message</MudText>
            }

            <MudStack Spacing="3" Class="elicitation-card-fields">
                @foreach (ElicitationField field in current.Form.Fields)
                {
                    ElicitationField shown = field;
                    ElicitationField? companion = CompanionOf(current.Form, shown);
                    bool optionsDisabled = busy || this.CompanionFilled(current, companion);
                    bool labelHidden = HidesLabel(current.Form, shown);
                    bool isSelect = shown.Kind is ElicitationFieldKind.SingleSelect or ElicitationFieldKind.MultiSelect;
                    string? shownLabel = labelHidden ? null : shown.Label;
                    string? loneName = labelHidden && !isSelect ? current.Form.NameOf(shown) : null;

                    if (shown.CustomAnswerFor is null)
                    {
                        <div @key="shown.Key" class="elicitation-card-field" role="@(loneName is null ? null : "group")" aria-label="@loneName">
                            @switch (shown.Kind)
                            {
                                case ElicitationFieldKind.Date:
                                    <MudDatePicker Label="@shownLabel"
                                                   HelperText="@shown.Description"
                                                   Required="@shown.Required"
                                                   Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                   Editable="true"
                                                   DateFormat="yyyy-MM-dd"
                                                   Culture="@CultureInfo.InvariantCulture"
                                                   Disabled="@busy"
                                                   Date="@this.DateOf(current, shown)"
                                                   DateChanged="@(date => this.SetDate(current, shown, date))" />
                                    break;

                                case ElicitationFieldKind.Boolean:
                                    <MudSwitch T="bool"
                                               Color="Color.Primary"
                                               Required="@shown.Required"
                                               Disabled="@busy"
                                               Value="@(this.EntryOf(current, shown) == "true")"
                                               ValueChanged="@(on => this.SetBoolean(current, shown, on))">
                                        @if (!labelHidden)
                                        {
                                            <span class="elicitation-card-field-label">@shown.Label</span>
                                        }
                                        @if (shown.Required)
                                        {
                                            <span class="elicitation-card-required" aria-hidden="true"> *</span>
                                        }
                                    </MudSwitch>
                                    if (shown.Description is not null)
                                    {
                                        <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="elicitation-card-field-description">@shown.Description</MudText>
                                    }

                                    break;

                                case ElicitationFieldKind.SingleSelect:
                                    <div role="group" aria-label="@current.Form.NameOf(shown)" aria-required="@(shown.Required ? "true" : null)" class="elicitation-card-group">
                                        @Heading(shown, !labelHidden)
                                        <MudRadioGroup T="string"
                                                       Disabled="@optionsDisabled"
                                                       Value="@this.EntryOf(current, shown)"
                                                       ValueChanged="@(value => this.SetSingle(current, shown, value))">
                                            @foreach (ElicitationOption option in shown.Options)
                                            {
                                                <MudRadio @key="option.Value" T="string" Value="@option.Value" Color="Color.Primary" Class="elicitation-card-option">
                                                    <span class="elicitation-card-option-label">@option.Label</span>@if (option.Description is not null)
                                                    {
                                                        <span class="elicitation-card-option-description">@option.Description</span>
                                                    }
                                                </MudRadio>
                                            }
                                        </MudRadioGroup>
                                    </div>
                                    break;

                                case ElicitationFieldKind.MultiSelect:
                                    <div role="group" aria-label="@current.Form.NameOf(shown)" aria-required="@(shown.Required ? "true" : null)" class="elicitation-card-group">
                                        @Heading(shown, !labelHidden)
                                        <MudStack Spacing="0" AlignItems="AlignItems.Start">
                                            @foreach (ElicitationOption option in shown.Options)
                                            {
                                                string value = option.Value;
                                                <MudCheckBox @key="value" T="bool"
                                                             Color="Color.Primary"
                                                             Class="elicitation-card-option"
                                                             Disabled="@optionsDisabled"
                                                             Value="@this.IsTicked(current, shown, value)"
                                                             ValueChanged="@(on => this.SetTicked(current, shown, value, on))">
                                                    <span class="elicitation-card-option-label">@option.Label</span>@if (option.Description is not null)
                                                    {
                                                        <span class="elicitation-card-option-description">@option.Description</span>
                                                    }
                                                </MudCheckBox>
                                            }
                                        </MudStack>
                                    </div>
                                    break;

                                default:
                                    string? problem = ProblemOf(shown, this.EntriesOf(current));
                                    <MudTextField T="string"
                                                  Label="@shownLabel"
                                                  HelperText="@HelperTextOf(shown)"
                                                  Error="@(problem is not null)"
                                                  ErrorText="@problem"
                                                  Required="@shown.Required"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                  Immediate="true"
                                                  InputMode="@InputModeOf(shown.Kind)"
                                                  Disabled="@busy"
                                                  Value="@this.EntryOf(current, shown)"
                                                  ValueChanged="@(text => this.SetText(current, shown, text))" />
                                    break;
                            }

                            @if (companion is { } other)
                            {
                                <MudTextField T="string"
                                              Label="@other.Label"
                                              HelperText="@other.Description"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Immediate="true"
                                              Disabled="@busy"
                                              Class="elicitation-card-other"
                                              Value="@this.EntryOf(current, other)"
                                              ValueChanged="@(text => this.SetText(current, other, text))" />
                            }
                        </div>
                    }
                }
            </MudStack>

            <MudStack Row="true" Spacing="2" Class="elicitation-card-actions">
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Class="elicitation-card-send"
                           Disabled="@(busy || !this.CanSend(current))"
                           OnClick="@(() => this.SendAsync(current))">@(busy ? "Sending…" : "Send")</MudButton>
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Class="elicitation-card-skip"
                           Disabled="@busy"
                           OnClick="@(() => this.SkipAsync(current))">Skip</MudButton>
            </MudStack>
        </MudPaper>
    }
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The Room whose waiting forms, if any, this card shows.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string RoomId { get; set; } = "";

    private string? loadedRoomId;
    private Room? room;
    private IReadOnlyList<PendingElicitation> cards = [];
    private readonly HashSet<string> busyIds = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    // What the Human has entered, by card id and then field key: the shape ElicitationComposer reads. A
    // card's entry is dropped when the card leaves the Room, so only a card whose id changed starts empty.
    private readonly Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, List<string>>> entered = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    /// <summary>Subscribes to <see cref="RoomEvents.ElicitationsChanged"/>, unsubscribed in <see cref="Dispose"/> per rules.md.</summary>
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        this.Events.ElicitationsChanged += this.OnElicitationsChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>Reloads this card's Room and waiting forms whenever <see cref="RoomId"/> changes - a component reused across Rooms.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (this.RoomId == this.loadedRoomId)
        {
            return;
        }

        this.loadedRoomId = this.RoomId;
        this.room = await this.TeamDirectory.GetRoomAsync(this.RoomId);
        this.Show(this.Elicitations.Get(this.RoomId));
    }

    /// <summary>Unsubscribes - the hub is a singleton, so a component that does not unsubscribe here never dies.</summary>
    public void Dispose()
    {
        this.Events.ElicitationsChanged -= this.OnElicitationsChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Shows <paramref name="next"/>, the cards now waiting, in the order the store lists them. What the
    /// Human entered is kept for every card still waiting and dropped for every card that is gone, so an
    /// entry resets only when its own card's id changes.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="next">The cards now waiting, oldest first.</param>
    private void Show(IReadOnlyList<PendingElicitation> next)
    {
        HashSet<string> waiting = [.. next.Select(static card => card.Id)];
        foreach (string gone in this.entered.Keys.Where(id => !waiting.Contains(id)).ToList())
        {
            _ = this.entered.Remove(gone);
        }

        this.cards = next;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Reacts to <see cref="RoomEvents.ElicitationsChanged"/> for this card's own Room - ignored while an
    /// answer is in flight, because that is this card's own answer taking its card; the click handler's
    /// <c>finally</c> block refreshes once the call returns.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="roomId">The Room whose waiting forms changed.</param>
    private void OnElicitationsChanged(string roomId)
    {
        if (!string.Equals(roomId, this.RoomId, StringComparison.Ordinal) || this.busyIds.Count > 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        _ = this.DispatchAsync(() =>
        {
            this.Show(this.Elicitations.Get(this.RoomId));
            this.StateHasChanged();
            return Task.CompletedTask;
        });
    }

    /// <summary>Whether an answer for <paramref name="card"/> is in flight.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    private bool IsBusy(PendingElicitation card)
    {
        return this.busyIds.Contains(card.Id);
    }

    /// <summary>Whether <see cref="ElicitationComposer"/> says the values entered into <paramref name="card"/> may be sent.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    private bool CanSend(PendingElicitation card)
    {
        return ElicitationComposer.CanSend(card.Form, this.SnapshotOf(card));
    }

    /// <summary>The values entered into <paramref name="card"/> in the composer's shape: filled fields only.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    private Dictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<string>> SnapshotOf(PendingElicitation card)
    {
        Dictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<string>> values = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);
        foreach ((string key, List<string> entries) in this.EntriesOf(card))
        {
            if (entries.Count > 0)
            {
                values[key] = [.. entries];
            }
        }

        return values;
    }

    /// <summary>The entries the Human has made into <paramref name="card"/>, created empty on first use.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    private Dictionary<string, List<string>> EntriesOf(PendingElicitation card)
    {
        if (!this.entered.TryGetValue(card.Id, out Dictionary<string, List<string>>? entries))
        {
            entries = new Dictionary<string, List<string>>(StringComparer.Ordinal);
            this.entered[card.Id] = entries;
        }

        return entries;
    }

    /// <summary>The single entry of a scalar field, or the empty string when there is none.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The field.</param>
    private string EntryOf(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField field)
    {
        return this.EntriesOf(card).TryGetValue(field.Key, out List<string>? entries) && entries.Count > 0 ? entries[0] : string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>The "Other" field typed in place of <paramref name="field"/>'s selection, or <see langword="null"/>.</summary>
    /// <param name="form">The form.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The field that may be a question.</param>
    private static ElicitationField? CompanionOf(ElicitationForm form, ElicitationField field)
    {
        return form.Fields.FirstOrDefault(candidate => string.Equals(candidate.CustomAnswerFor, field.Key, StringComparison.Ordinal));
    }

    /// <summary>Whether the Human has typed a non-blank custom answer into <paramref name="companion"/>, which makes it beat its question's options.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="companion">The "Other" field, or <see langword="null"/> when the field has none.</param>
    private bool CompanionFilled(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField? companion)
    {
        return companion is not null && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(this.EntryOf(card, companion));
    }

    /// <summary>The keyboard hint for a text-like field: a number brings up a numeric pad, an integer a digits-only one.</summary>
    /// <param name="kind">The field's kind.</param>
    private static InputMode InputModeOf(ElicitationFieldKind kind)
    {
        return kind switch
        {
            ElicitationFieldKind.Integer => InputMode.numeric,
            ElicitationFieldKind.Number => InputMode.@decimal,
            _ => InputMode.text,
        };
    }

    /// <summary>Stores what was typed into a text-like field. Typing a custom answer clears the selection it stands in for.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The field typed into.</param>
    /// <param name="text">The text now in the input.</param>
    private void SetText(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField field, string? text)
    {
        Dictionary<string, List<string>> entries = this.EntriesOf(card);
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(text))
        {
            _ = entries.Remove(field.Key);
            return;
        }

        entries[field.Key] = [text];
        if (field.CustomAnswerFor is { } target && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(text))
        {
            _ = entries.Remove(target);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Stores the option chosen in a single select.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The single select.</param>
    /// <param name="value">The chosen option's value.</param>
    private void SetSingle(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField field, string? value)
    {
        Dictionary<string, List<string>> entries = this.EntriesOf(card);
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value))
        {
            _ = entries.Remove(field.Key);
            return;
        }

        entries[field.Key] = [value];
    }

    /// <summary>Whether <paramref name="optionValue"/> is among the options ticked in a multi select.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The multi select.</param>
    /// <param name="optionValue">The option's value.</param>
    private bool IsTicked(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField field, string optionValue)
    {
        return this.EntriesOf(card).TryGetValue(field.Key, out List<string>? entries) && entries.Contains(optionValue, StringComparer.Ordinal);
    }

    /// <summary>Ticks or unticks one option of a multi select.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The multi select.</param>
    /// <param name="optionValue">The option's value.</param>
    /// <param name="ticked">Whether it is now ticked.</param>
    private void SetTicked(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField field, string optionValue, bool ticked)
    {
        Dictionary<string, List<string>> entries = this.EntriesOf(card);
        List<string> chosen = entries.TryGetValue(field.Key, out List<string>? existing) ? existing : [];
        _ = chosen.RemoveAll(entry => string.Equals(entry, optionValue, StringComparison.Ordinal));
        if (ticked)
        {
            chosen.Add(optionValue);
        }

        if (chosen.Count == 0)
        {
            _ = entries.Remove(field.Key);
            return;
        }

        entries[field.Key] = chosen;
    }

    /// <summary>Stores a switch: <c>true</c> or <c>false</c>, exactly what <see cref="ElicitationComposer"/> reads.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The boolean field.</param>
    /// <param name="on">Whether the switch is on.</param>
    private void SetBoolean(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField field, bool on)
    {
        this.EntriesOf(card)[field.Key] = [on ? "true" : "false"];
    }

    /// <summary>The date a date field currently holds, for the picker; <see langword="null"/> when none or not a valid <c>yyyy-MM-dd</c>.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The date field.</param>
    private DateTime? DateOf(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField field)
    {
        return DateOnly.TryParseExact(this.EntryOf(card, field), "yyyy-MM-dd", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out DateOnly date)
            ? date.ToDateTime(TimeOnly.MinValue)
            : null;
    }

    /// <summary>Stores a picked date as ISO <c>yyyy-MM-dd</c> text, whatever the machine's culture; no date clears the field.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The date field.</param>
    /// <param name="date">The picked date, or <see langword="null"/>.</param>
    private void SetDate(PendingElicitation card, ElicitationField field, DateTime? date)
    {
        Dictionary<string, List<string>> entries = this.EntriesOf(card);
        if (date is null)
        {
            _ = entries.Remove(field.Key);
            return;
        }

        entries[field.Key] = [date.Value.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)];
    }

    /// <summary>Whether <paramref name="field"/> is shown with no label because the form's message is the only name it has (a lone field labelled by nothing but its key).</summary>
    /// <param name="form">The form.</param>
    /// <param name="field">The field.</param>
    private static bool HidesLabel(ElicitationForm form, ElicitationField field)
    {
        return form.MessageStandsInForLabel && string.Equals(form.SoleField?.Key, field.Key, StringComparison.Ordinal);
    }

    /// <summary>The text under a text-like input: the field's own description, then the range a number may take, on separate lines; <see langword="null"/> when it has neither.</summary>
    /// <param name="field">The field.</param>
    private static string? HelperTextOf(ElicitationField field)
    {
        string[] lines = [.. new[] { field.Description, ElicitationComposer.RangeHint(field) }.Where(static line => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(line)).OfType<string>()];
        return lines.Length == 0 ? null : string.Join('\n', lines);
    }

    /// <summary>Why the number or integer typed into <paramref name="field"/> cannot be sent, as <see cref="ElicitationComposer"/> words it; <see langword="null"/> for any other field, an empty one or a valid value.</summary>
    /// <param name="field">The field.</param>
    /// <param name="entries">What the Human has entered into the card, by field key.</param>
    private static string? ProblemOf(ElicitationField field, Dictionary<string, List<string>> entries)
    {
        return (field.Kind is ElicitationFieldKind.Number or ElicitationFieldKind.Integer) && entries.TryGetValue(field.Key, out List<string>? typed)
            ? ElicitationComposer.CheckField(field, typed)
            : null;
    }

    /// <summary>The heading of a select: its header, its label (when it is shown) with a required mark, and its description, all as plain text.</summary>
    /// <param name="field">The select.</param>
    /// <param name="showLabel">Whether to show the label; a select the message names has none, and keeps only its required mark.</param>
    private static RenderFragment Heading(ElicitationField field, bool showLabel)
    {
        return @<div class="elicitation-card-field-head">
            @if (field.Header is not null)
            {
                <MudText Typo="Typo.overline" Class="elicitation-card-field-header">@field.Header</MudText>
            }
            @if (showLabel || field.Required)
            {
                <div class="elicitation-card-field-heading">
                    @if (showLabel)
                    {
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="elicitation-card-field-label">@field.Label</MudText>
                    }
                    @if (field.Required)
                    {
                        <span class="elicitation-card-required" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
                    }
                </div>
            }
            @if (field.Description is not null)
            {
                <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="elicitation-card-field-description">@field.Description</MudText>
            }
        </div>;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Sends the answer through the real <see cref="ElicitationService"/>. The outcome is the posted
    /// Message, never card state, so this only refreshes what is still waiting once the call returns.
    /// <see cref="CancellationToken.None"/> on purpose: once the card is taken, abandoning the post when a
    /// circuit drops would lose the answer. The one documented failure, <see cref="InvalidOperationException"/>
    /// (the values do not fit the form, a UI bug), is shown through <see cref="ISnackbar"/> and the card
    /// stays waiting; <see cref="ElicitationService"/> turns every posting failure into a quiet result itself.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card being answered.</param>
    private async Task SendAsync(PendingElicitation card)
    {
        if (this.IsBusy(card))
        {
            return;
        }

        _ = this.busyIds.Add(card.Id);
        try
        {
            _ = await this.Service.AnswerAsync(this.RoomId, card.Id, this.SnapshotOf(card), CancellationToken.None);
        }
        catch (InvalidOperationException ex)
        {
            this.Snackbar.Add(ex.Message, Severity.Error);
        }
        finally
        {
            _ = this.busyIds.Remove(card.Id);
            this.Show(this.Elicitations.Get(this.RoomId));
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Skips the card: the waiting request is declined, nothing is posted and the asker is not woken.</summary>
    /// <param name="card">The card being skipped.</param>
    private async Task SkipAsync(PendingElicitation card)
    {
        if (this.IsBusy(card))
        {
            return;
        }

        _ = await this.Service.DeclineAsync(this.RoomId, card.Id);
        this.Show(this.Elicitations.Get(this.RoomId));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Marshals <paramref name="action"/> onto this component's renderer, matching <c>QuestionCard</c>'s own
    /// <c>DispatchAsync</c> - a stale subscription firing after this card has already been disposed (a Room
    /// switch, a closed circuit) must not throw.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="action">The state update and repaint to run on the renderer.</param>
    private async Task DispatchAsync(Func<Task> action)
    {
        try
        {
            await this.InvokeAsync(action);
        }
        catch (ObjectDisposedException)
        {
            // Circuit gone; nothing to render.
        }
        catch (InvalidOperationException)
        {
            // Renderer disposed mid-dispatch.
        }
    }
}
